{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"**No.** As of November 6, 2026, appointing a principal underwriter does not, by itself, assure a sales force, investor demand, or asset gathering.\n\n- **Legal/operational distribution:** The distributor generally serves as the registered broker-dealer for the ETF’s continuous offering. Depending on its agreement, responsibilities can include creation-unit distribution arrangements, authorized-participant agreements, and advertising compliance review. These functions are not equivalent to active selling.\n- **Commercial distribution:** Wholesaling, advisor outreach, lead generation, marketing campaigns, and sales support must be expressly included or separately contracted. Intermediary selling agreements, platform admission, due diligence, and shelf access are distinct; neither appointment nor access guarantees recommendations or flows.\n\nSeries-trust platforms differ: some bundle meaningful commercial support; others provide principally regulatory and operational infrastructure. Examine the actual contracts, staffing commitments, deliverables, fees, and exclusions.\n\n**Worth knowing:** “Distributor appointed” is not the same as “distribution secured.”"}}
